{
	title: 'Terminal: completion list below the prompt, monochrome in screen',
	spec: "Tab completion shows its choices as a list below the prompt, as the old Hal did: one line of names separated by spaces (directories with a trailing /), wrapping to more lines as needed, gone after the next key; choices are not browsed, so Up and Down keep recalling history. Inside GNU screen (STY set, or TERM starting with 'screen') the terminal is monochrome: no colours at all and no kitty keyboard query, keeping only bold, dim and reverse video for the cursor, selection and status; no emulated palette. Prompt placeholders (task 8m) also show on the web prompt, where they are missing today.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Choices are app.state.choices (one list, not per tab): deleted at the top of every key in onKeys and on a tab switch (tab-switch.ts), so Up after Tab recalls history. frame.build draws them below the prompt box as chrome, joined by two spaces and word-wrapped, so the padding lifts the prompt rather than pushing rows off. The web still shows choices as its notice.',
		"Monochrome: ansi.mono() reads STY and TERM on every call; ansi.sgr returns '' then, which removes every colour (paint, tab bar, modal) in one place, and terminal.kitty() is !ansi.mono(). The modal's selected row falls back to reverse video. ./test unsets STY and a screen TERM so tests run in colour inside screen.",
